 HALT:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C halt() - terminate the program through the Pascal runtime.
C
C Calling convention for a zero-argument ASSEMBLER routine:
C   M13 = return link (discarded -- halt() never returns)
C   M1  = runtime constant base
C   M7  = top of the Pascal activation chain (kept current by the runtime)
C
C This is the Pascal runtime's P/HT (paslib/p_ht.asm), inlined instead of
C tail-called:
C   1. Invoke the user's post-mortem-dump entry if one was installed at
C      PASPMDAD -- the same cell name and convention C/AH already uses.
C   2. Call C/RC to walk back up the activation chain rooted at M7,
C      running any cleanup linked from each frame's state word at
C      mem[M7+1].
C   3. Patch the address field of the outermost frame's state word so
C      the eventual frame-return jumps to STOP*, the runtime's final
C      exit.  mem[M7+1] is a *data* slot in the activation frame, never
C      an instruction in program text, so this is not self-modifying
C      code.
C   4. Dispatch to P/E (normal end) or P/EF (forced end, runs the
C      patched cleanup) depending on whether the outer frame carried one.
C===========================================================
 PASPMDAD:,LC,1              . user post-mortem-dump entry, or 0
 STOP*:,SUBP,                . runtime final exit (MS Dubna OS)
 C/E:,SUBP,                  . normal Pascal end-of-program
 C/RC:,SUBP,                 . activation-chain unwinder (in longjmp)
 C/EF:,SUBP,                 . forced end (runs patched cleanup)
 14,VTM,PASPMDAD             . M14 := &PASPMDAD
 14,XTA,                     . ACC := PASPMDAD
 ,UZA,NOPMD                  . none installed -> skip PMD
 13,VTM,NOPMD                . arrange PMD to return here
 14,WTC,                     . C := PASPMDAD
 ,UJ,                        . jump into the PMD handler
 NOPMD:1,MTJ,13              . M13 := M1 (chain-end sentinel for C/RC:
C                              it stops when M7 == saved M13)
 14,VJM,C/RC                 . unwind the activation chain
 7,XTA,1                     . ACC := mem[M7+1] = outer frame's
C                              state/return-link word
 ,UTC,ADDRMASK.=77 7770 0000 . C := address of high-bits mask
 ,AAX,                       . ACC &= mask (clear address field, keep
C                              cleanup/opcode bits)
 14,VTM,STOP*                . M14 := STOP*
 ,ITS,14                     . push STOP* onto the BESM-6 stack
 15,AOX,-1                   . ACC |= mem[SP-1] = STOP* (install STOP*
C                              as the new address part)
 7,STX,1                     . store patched link; pop saved high part
C                              into ACC
 ,UZA,C/E                    . saved cleanup/opcode part zero -> C/E
 ,UJ,C/EF                    . else hand off to C/EF
 ADDRMASK:,LOG,77 7770 0000  . high-bits mask (clears the address field)
 ,END,
